      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Surfinia, Wave and Million Bells are trade series; Calibrachoa (Million Bells) is a different genus. Watering: Texas Tech says moist well-drained soil with medium water need, RHS moist but well-drained, NC State good drainage and moist with moderate drought tolerance; no page gives a schedule, so keep_moist is the agent's mapping and the interval is a guess for pots in summer. Light: RHS full sun; NC State full sun to partial shade (survives heavy shade, flowers poorly); Texas Tech lists light shade, so it differs. Size from Texas Tech (8 to 15 in tall, 1 to 3 ft spread, upper values); NC State agrees on spread. Habit and growth rate: NC State's care-attribute part came through a summary of a truncated page (rapid, spreading), so both are marked as the agent's reading; cultivar groups range from mounding to trailing. The RHS page is for the cultivar 'Wave Purple', not the species. Toxicity: ASPCA lists Petunia as non-toxic to dogs and cats (fact only, own words), NC State tags it non-toxic; neither gives symptoms, so no child or adult line is stored. Humidity and temperature: no usable figure. The University of Minnesota Extension petunia page returned 403 and was not used."
      },
